The graph crosses the y- axis at the point $$\left( {0,-6} \right)$$. The y- intercept is $$\left( {0,-6} \right)$$.</item>
          <item>ⓒ The graph crosses the x- axis at the point $$\left( {-5,0} \right)$$. The x- intercept is $$\left( {-5,0} \right)$$.
The graph crosses the y- axis at the point $$\left( {0,-5} \right)$$. The y- intercept is $$\left( {0,-5} \right)$$.</item>
        </list>
      </solution>
    </example>
