      <problem>
        <p>Road trip. Damien is driving from Chicago to Denver, a distance of 1000 miles. The x- axis on the graph below shows the time in hours since Damien left Chicago. The y- axis represents the distance he has left to drive.</p>
        <list type="ol" style="1">
          <item>ⓐ Find the x- and y- intercepts.</item>
          <item>ⓑ Explain what the x- and y- intercepts mean for Damien.</item>
        </list>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <p>ⓐ $$\left( {0,1000} \right),\left( {15,0} \right)$$
ⓑ At $$\left( {0,1000} \right)$$, he has been gone 0 hours and has 1000 miles left. At $$\left( {15,0} \right)$$, he has been gone 15 hours and has 0 miles left to go.</p>
      </solution>
